TEST809_ROW {"case_id": "Q3_PARA", "question": "Separate guidance about data discovery from observations about links that actually work.", "adaptive": {"action": "ANSWER", "answer": "The first pillar of FAIR is Findable, ensuring data is uniquely identified with a persistent identifier (PID) like a DOI, which is tracked by resources such as DataCite. In a study of PLOS ONE, 80% of resources could be retrieved automatically, with 98% of DOIs successfully leading to the resource when manually tested.", "policy": "ADAPTIVE", "selected": ["PMC9521804", "PMC9401135"], "steps": [{"operation": "INITIAL", "ids": ["PMC9521804"], "raw": "Findable data should have a persistent identifier (PID) like a DOI, which is machine-readable and allows for discovery by search engines. Accessible data must be retrievable using a standard protocol, ensuring the links actually work.", "tokens": 46, "max_new": 128, "possible_truncation": false, "sentence_end": true, "sdpa_calls": 184, "elapsed_seconds": 11.031}, {"operation": "FUSE_TO_VERIFY_FIRST", "ids": ["PMC9521804", "PMC9401135"], "raw": "The first pillar of FAIR is Findable, ensuring data is uniquely identified with a persistent identifier (PID) like a DOI, which is tracked by resources such as DataCite. In a study of PLOS ONE, 80% of resources could be retrieved automatically, with 98% of DOIs successfully leading to the resource when manually tested.", "tokens": 74, "max_new": 128, "possible_truncation": false, "sentence_end": true, "sdpa_calls": 296, "elapsed_seconds": 22.086}, {"operation": "REVERSE_CHECK", "ids": ["PMC9401135", "PMC9521804"], "raw": "The first pillar of FAIR is Findable, ensuring data is uniquely identified with a persistent identifier (PID) like a DOI. However, even with a PID, the actual link to the data may become invalid over time due to link rot and content drift.", "tokens": 53, "max_new": 128, "possible_truncation": false, "sentence_end": true, "sdpa_calls": 212, "elapsed_seconds": 19.201}], "trace": [{"ste